    "notes": "Model: owner-FCF DCF, component build, 10-year horizon, scenario-weighted. Routed via dcf-methods SKILL.md as a US operating company (diversified industrial, cyclical end markets: auto builds, industrial capex, food service, residential renovation); not a bank/REIT/holdco/LIC. First valuation of ITW -- no prior DCF and no memory entry. FY0 is FY2025 (revenue $16,044M, operating income $4,216M = 26.3%, D&A $397M = depreciation 317 + amortization 80, capex $419M). Adj. EBITDA margin in the paths is pre-SBC (operating income + D&A + SBC): FY2025 29.2%. Year 1 (FY2026) anchored to Q3-2026 guidance (Oct 27, 2026): revenue +4.5-5.5% (9M actual +5.0%), operating margin 26.5-27.5% -> 27.0% + D&A 2.4% + SBC 0.45% = 29.9% adj. EBITDA. Interest income ($40M FY2025) NOT stripped: ITW carries ~$8.6B net debt, so no net-cash double count arises. Net debt at 30 Sep 2026: total debt $9,372M (short-term $2,219M incl. commercial paper and Nov-2026 notes + long-term $7,153M) less cash $809M. Working capital capture negative (-15% of the revenue change): receivables + inventory (~$4.8B) far exceed payables, so growth consumes cash (9M 2026: receivables -$300M, inventories -$174M). Pension plans are modestly funded and not bridged. Buyback pace: $1.5B/yr FY2023-25, $1.31B in 9M 2026 (guide ~$1.5B); the flat count is therefore funded, not a convention. Cash tax 24% of EBIT: FY2025 cash taxes paid $1,052M vs book ETR 22.7%; FY2026 ETR guide 23-24% excluding discrete benefits.",
